  "limits": [
    "New regular trace layer binary has not been run in Diablo; latest real game proof remains diablo-camera-updates-v1.json source e8b2702. No game/HMD was launched in this milestone.",
    "The runtime pose source is an external diagnostic text file; supplied XR-like poses/time are not a real OpenXR observation or current display-time claim. No OpenXR call or SteamVR submission occurs in this layer mode.",
    "Same actual CaptureProjection adapter and Capture GPU leases are wired to the original-render layer cycle, with an isolated GPU-to-CPU readback consumer for verification. This is not the intended GPU-only XR presentation path.",
    "All views are successive, keep distinct original capture/present IDs and sceneSequence zero. Whole scene, simultaneous time, game optical/depth projection and continuous immersive stereo are unverified.",
    "The tagged WSI shader retains its original projection and exercises requested eye/game-view translation. Real Diablo projection/clip/scale conventions must be calibrated before a new game-to-XR trial.",
    "Foreign-producer WSI fixture uses explicit application timeline ordering and a host acquisition fence. Clean final synchronization validation does not prove asynchronous multiqueue game/runtime coordination; earlier insufficient fixture acquisition paths are not part of this proof.",
    "Normal layer path polls its consumer fence; file reads, CPU copies/private exports and teardown can block. A request without an admissible left image has no automatic timeout; pose.stop or game/device teardown cancels it.",
    "Common diagnostic codec/consumer compile under Windows in CI, but native Windows D3D12 game/VR integration and physical SteamVR validation issues remain unresolved."
